      <h1 id="network-observability-scheduling-resources" class="group scroll-mt-20">Scheduling resources<a href="#network-observability-scheduling-resources" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Taints and tolerations help you control which nodes host certain pods. Use these tools, along with node selectors, to guide the placement of network observability components.</p>
      <p>A node selector specifies a map of key/value pairs that are defined using custom labels on nodes and selectors specified in pods.</p>
      <p>For the pod to be eligible to run on a node, the pod must have the same key/value node selector as the label on the node.</p>
      <h2 id="network-observability-multi-tenancy_network_observability_scheduling" class="group scroll-mt-20">Network observability deployment in specific nodes<a href="#network-observability-multi-tenancy_network_observability_scheduling" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Configure the <code>FlowCollector</code> resource using scheduling specifications, including <code>NodeSelector</code>, <code>Tolerations</code>, and <code>Affinity</code>, to control the deployment of network observability components on specific nodes.</p>
      <p>The <code>spec.agent.ebpf.advanced.scheduling</code>, <code>spec.processor.advanced.scheduling</code>, and <code>spec.consolePlugin.advanced.scheduling</code> specifications have the following configurable settings:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><code>NodeSelector</code></li>
      <li><code>Tolerations</code></li>
      <li><code>Affinity</code></li>
      <li><code>PriorityClassName</code></li>
      </ul>
